Source landscape: The 2023 documentary universe is broad and unusually well preserved across White House and presidential archives, statutes and congressional records, GAO/OIG audits, agency implementation documents, budgets, academic and think-tank assessments, reputable reporting, and international coverage. Major source families include Biden’s stated “Investing in America” and foreign-policy programs; implementation of infrastructure, CHIPS, IRA, broadband, and workforce initiatives; border, immigration, and administrative-capacity records; Ukraine, Afghanistan, NATO, and crisis management; and favorable, adverse, mixed, and exculpatory evaluations. Congressional pages produced access restrictions in search, so those records are retained as access-blocked or unopened candidates.

